{"event_type":"review","id":"8b98ebd7cd2068a6a385afab61d0c300cf3c9ddf9741dfedb50cef8857087567","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T16:16:46Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e89f5b7bcc3fd0a90b13eb741a4120eaf93f2ac5720f785b921f8972d98d7f74","sha256":"e89f5b7bcc3fd0a90b13eb741a4120eaf93f2ac5720f785b921f8972d98d7f74"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/aab7fc29ca0b3a04f5623774e6165362466c8445dcee4aa3b43b6025c2e6ec26","sha256":"aab7fc29ca0b3a04f5623774e6165362466c8445dcee4aa3b43b6025c2e6ec26"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/61a83e0ab1e5afa43c7a4dbd3b1cd9dbc353c126569ebc0ad4d326ca7dab7512","sha256":"61a83e0ab1e5afa43c7a4dbd3b1cd9dbc353c126569ebc0ad4d326ca7dab7512"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b1596f721d9842004203340d8de9e306e1eaf606ab01af977780a2f5a5dc53a1","sha256":"b1596f721d9842004203340d8de9e306e1eaf606ab01af977780a2f5a5dc53a1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/29748dba41c4866421e710d47eeea7b81a42bf60525e9db36616e849628a8939","sha256":"29748dba41c4866421e710d47eeea7b81a42bf60525e9db36616e849628a8939"}],"attempt_id":"2ec5472bdfd5d3f2be5aa8a4f4c38ac7a0087a7b0e7afceb0aff3b1d13b8a8d4:0:1","base":"e82e09015a6bc7d77d96db7100da9935feb80fe2","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"be498acd0bf11c3988816549d54319a45af04d81","body":"**Correct the token-scoping guidance for repository creation.**\n\nThe recommended token cannot be limited to a newly named scratch repository before that repository exists: GitHub’s selected-repository token setup requires selecting repositories when the token is created. The drill also needs repository-creation permission. Document a credential that can create the repository and access it afterward, or separate creation from the repo-scoped drill credential. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/managing-your-personal-access-tokens))","id":"19a83ea2875dbf5817e33faa4a052148cb00b27d9c0a4b3593e5e824d78d230f","intervals":[],"path":".github/workflows/live-review.yml","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Correct the token-scoping guidance for repository creation."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"17d84601b6e508aff140c9821743de9f5e6c6297","body":"**Queue every requested live run.**\n\nIf one run is active and two more are dispatched, GitHub cancels the first pending run despite `cancel-in-progress: false`. Add `queue: max` if each manual dispatch must produce a drill result. The current setting preserves the active run, but not every queued run. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-when-workflows-run/control-workflow-concurrency?utm_source=openai))\n\n  \n<details>\n<summary>Proposed change</summary>\n\n```diff\n concurrency:\n   group: live-drivers\n+  queue: max\n   cancel-in-progress: false\n```\n</details>","id":"207293c6ee5b4d28fcb2755520bab78ff6f49af86e3fd8e993dd73cd68536164","intervals":[],"path":".github/workflows/live-drivers.yml","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Queue every requested live run."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"17d84601b6e508aff140c9821743de9f5e6c6297","body":"**Limit provider secrets to the live steps.**\n\nJob-level `env` gives both provider keys to every step, including dependency installation and the build. If code run by either step is compromised, it can read keys before a live check starts. Set the keys on only the live steps that need them. GitHub makes job-level variables available to all steps and supports step-level variables. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud%40latest/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax?utm_source=openai))","id":"c12ddf3a03476d7a58c8987796093df34401fdd97584a7801ad363ad8b33cc72","intervals":[],"path":".github/workflows/live-drivers.yml","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Limit provider secrets to the live steps."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"1183b08885a92929deb7025c46baf58dee0b16f9","body":"**Keep `pack-audit.yml` identical to its template.**\n\n`.github/workflows/pack-audit.yml:25` differs from its source template. The instance reads `test/scripts/packed-smoke.test.ts mocks/fixture-tests it`, while `policy/templates/pack-audit.yml:25` reads `test/scripts/packed-smoke.*.test.ts mock/fixture-test it`. The mapping in `policy/templates/instances.json` (lines 90-91) identifies that template as the source for this workflow. Repository guidance says workflows under `.github/workflows/` are never edited directly. A later re-instantiation overwrites this direct edit.\n\nEdit `policy/templates/pack-audit.yml` if the template wording is the intended one, then re-instantiate the workflow. If the instance wording is intended, change the template first and re-instantiate it.","id":"2e26f5eb78d749ba84f00a4a347b6aaea7d2bfec3e2ff86b61f96c5762614fa7","intervals":[],"path":".github/workflows/pack-audit.yml","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep `pack-audit.yml` identical to its template."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"a797e0390811e9229cc1924b0e1645e473329663","body":"**Re-instantiate the generated workflow from the template.**\n\nAt `.github/workflows/live-merge.yml:124`, the unescaped space causes a Bash syntax error before the step runs, including when `TEST_FILTER` is empty. The template already contains the escaped space at `policy/templates/live-merge.yml:123`; regenerate the workflow instead of editing the template again.","id":"23034e869142d2faa15f95aed04fed09b8b871da4107234201a8406805756347","intervals":[],"path":".github/workflows/live-merge.yml","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Re-instantiate the generated workflow from the template."}],"head":"00380dc2534a7d6326b0648c1588491cbdc1285f","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"a4ca61c059528397bf70cb1b91ce5fb6bd5637e7","intervals":[[1,109]],"path":".github/workflows/ci.yml"},{"blob":"41f4b151b71e5bceda9f2d941a9496233b76283b","intervals":[[1,133]],"path":".github/workflows/cq-measure.yml"},{"blob":"1a47befec8d2367658a79aeee9d3bb003dc53a44","intervals":[[1,132]],"path":".github/workflows/install-matrix.yml"},{"blob":"17d84601b6e508aff140c9821743de9f5e6c6297","intervals":[[1,104]],"path":".github/workflows/live-drivers.yml"},{"blob":"a797e0390811e9229cc1924b0e1645e473329663","intervals":[[1,128]],"path":".github/workflows/live-merge.yml"},{"blob":"be498acd0bf11c3988816549d54319a45af04d81","intervals":[[1,115]],"path":".github/workflows/live-review.yml"},{"blob":"1183b08885a92929deb7025c46baf58dee0b16f9","intervals":[[1,192]],"path":".github/workflows/pack-audit.yml"},{"blob":"bfc39980deee1963a686a4ff1e76a9d2dabbc322","intervals":[[1,132]],"path":".github/workflows/ratchet-propose-measure.yml"}],"job_id":"2ec5472bdfd5d3f2be5aa8a4f4c38ac7a0087a7b0e7afceb0aff3b1d13b8a8d4:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"a4ca61c059528397bf70cb1b91ce5fb6bd5637e7","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":".github/workflows/ci.yml","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"41f4b151b71e5bceda9f2d941a9496233b76283b","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":".github/workflows/cq-measure.yml","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"1a47befec8d2367658a79aeee9d3bb003dc53a44","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":".github/workflows/install-matrix.yml","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason